{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Moses commanded us a Torah.</b> This is what one generation to the next asks and says: thus we have transmitted from the mouth of Moses — an inheritance in our hands. And it is read by the mem-samekh-dalet [as] לנו [that which] draws himself and others after him. And likewise it is מורשה [an inheritance] to the congregation of Jacob, like והנבואה עודד הנביא. And it was מורשה מורשה [an inheritance, an inheritance], the congregation of Jacob."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The verse citation 'והנבואה עודד הנביא' (2 Chron. 15:8) is presented as a parallel for the construct-like chain; the phrase 'ויהי מורשה מורשה קהלת יעקב' restates the end of Deut. 33:4 with doubled מורשה, possibly reflecting a midrashic reading; the syntax is compressed and the final colon is rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:29.469672246Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}